= Prime-field index calculus: arity and solver correction
*DEC-20261031-b51282*

#image("diagram.svg", width: 100%)

The programme now treats every accepted arity-two theorem cell as component evidence, not as an exponent-changing ECDLP result. With $s = log_2(p)/m$, PDP work $2^(e s)$ and $Theta(2^s)$ required relations, collection costs $p^((e+1)/m)$ up to polynomial factors. Strict improvement on rho requires

#align(center)[*$e < m/2 - 1$.*]

At $m=2$ this requires $e<0$ and is impossible for nonnegative work. At $m=3$, the first relevant PDP screen, the necessary threshold is $e<0.5$. This is not sufficient for a complete index-calculus win: the retained PKM bridge still places its linear-algebra crossover at $m >= 4$.

== Correction boundaries

DEC-20261031-cd6460 remains the record of the standalone outer-chart metadata defect. DEC-20261031-ca1521 remains the fixed F5/F7 software evidence rejecting R1. This decision does not reopen either suite. It corrects the later inference: fixing the checker does not turn an $m=2$ component theorem into an ECDLP exponent result.

Boolean quotient equations $z^2-z$ avoid carry semantics in the mathematical field model, but a general bit-level $F_p$ multiplication still costs $Theta(log^2 p)$ gates. The theorem-bearing candidates are CaDiCaL with an external $F_p$ theory and independently replayed explanation clauses, plus a pinned cvc5 QF_FF export of the same predicate. Pure CNF reports encoding size and complete circuit cost only.

== Retained predicate

The corrected $m=3$ predicate uses three disjoint one-hot windows and two chained $S_3$ relations, never an expanded $S_4$. Its nonexceptional rational lift is

#align(center)[$(2 t lambda - s_0)^2 = f(x)$,]

with discriminant $16 t^2 f(x)$; $t=0$ remains an explicit exceptional branch. Under a rational non-2-torsion target, odd prime whole-group order and disjoint windows, the three-summand Frobenius argument supplies rationality. At arity four or higher explicit rationality circuits remain mandatory. Every out-of-domain field or index word receives a forbidden-word clause.

The Q1421 source bound to SHA-256 `0a0d2c673e9484f4b217917ee306e7663140e4d4618d8bb0ed8dc91947d08bc6` is an external-propagator precedent over $F_(2^n)$ only. It is not the missing $F_p$ theory.

== Fixed next measurement

Cryptanalysis PR #1343 fixes $m=3$, every integer $s=6..14$, and a strict Holm-corrected upper-interval gate $e<0.5$. Controls are exact two-window enumeration ($e=2$), a curve-free support-matched null, planted and exact-UNSAT instances, fresh-process A/A, and pure-CNF size accounting. Complete work includes target-dependent construction, theory work, explanation replay and independent group-law verification.

The 40--80-bit path is $s=13..27$, or about 39--81 field bits at $m=3$. The initial ladder reaches $s=13,14$; $s=15..27$ requires a separately frozen amendment. At 80 bits rho is about $2^40$ group operations, so this measures the PDP exponent rather than predicts a wall-clock win.

No $F_p$ propagator, held-out instance, cvc5 benchmark, field census or exponent fit exists in this correction. Scientific runs: zero. Performance claims: zero.

